.TH MAN 1
.SH NAME
man \- show a page of the manual
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B man
.RI [ section ]
.I name
.br
.B man
.B \-k
.I word
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B man
shows the page
.I name
of the manual, kept in
.BR /usr/share/man .
Without a
.IR section ,
it looks in sections 1, 8, 2, 4, 5 and 7, in that order, and shows the
first page found. A name that is not a page's file name is looked for in
the pages' NAME lines: a page may tell several commands
.RB ( "man pwd"
shows the page of
.BR cd ).
A
.I name
with a
.B /
in it is a file, shown as a page (to read one being written).
.PP
The words are filled to the width of the screen; bold and underlined words
use the terminal's attributes (on the PC's text screen: bright and cyan; a
terminal that has none shows plain text). A page longer than the screen is
shown a screen at a time; the last line tells where you are. The keys:
.TP
.BR space ", " f
the next screen
.TP
.B b
the screen before
.TP
.BR Enter ", " j ", " Down
one line on
.TP
.BR k ", " Up
one line back
.TP
.BR g ", " G
the top, the end
.TP
.BI / word
the next line with
.I word
(any case);
.B n
finds the next one
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl\-C
quit
.SS Sections
.TP
.B 1
commands: programs and the shell's built-in commands
.TP
.B 2
system calls: what the kernel offers
.TP
.B 4
servers and devices: the programs that drive the hardware and their messages
.TP
.B 5
file formats: the system's files
.TP
.B 7
overviews: the system as a whole
.TP
.B 8
administration: services, users, installing, the host tools
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-k " word"
List the pages whose names or one-line summary contain
.I word
(any case), as apropos does.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 1 if there is no such page (or nothing for
.BR \-k );
2 for a wrong command line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI /usr/share/man/ section / name . section
the pages, as written in man/ of SIEOS's sources, without their comments
.TP
.B /usr/share/man/whatis
every page's section, file, names and summary, one line each, made when
the disk is built
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
man sh
man 2 ipc_call
man \-k file
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (7),
.BR intro (7),
.BR help (1)
.SH BUGS
A terminal cannot tell its size yet: pages are filled to 78 columns and
shown 23 lines at a time. The desktop's terminal windows show no bold or
underline.
